# Build-context exclusions for Dockerfile.api.
#
# Dockerfile.api builds from the PARENT of this repo (it needs both dermiq/ and
# the sibling platform-core/), so the repo's own .dockerignore — which Docker
# resolves relative to the context root — never applies. BuildKit reads
# <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to the context-root one, which is how
# this file gets picked up from inside the repo. Patterns below are therefore
# relative to ~/projects, not to the repo.
#
# Without this, `COPY dermiq /build/dermiq/` swept in dermiq/.venv (1.8GB) and
# platform-core/.venv (430MB) and copied them into the image.

# Virtualenvs — the single biggest offender.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/env

# Python build artifacts
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/dist
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Secrets — must never enter the build context. Fly injects these as env vars.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p8
**/secrets
**/*secrets.env

# Everything the API image does not serve from.
frontend
airflow
transform
infra
docs
tests
scripts
**/node_modules
**/.next

# dbt + data artifacts
**/target
**/dbt_packages
**/logs
**/data
**/seed_output
**/*.csv
**/*.parquet
**/*.duckdb

# VCS / editor / OS noise
**/.git
**/.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
